  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Friday)\nIssued at 1221 PM MDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nUpper level ridge over the Rockies will shift east and expand \nover the central CONUS. This will result in very hot temperatures \nthis weekend into next week. Batches of mid level monsoon moisture\nwill advect through the region as near daily waves eject out of \nthe Rockies and into the FA. Upper level wave and trailing sfc \ntrough now progressing across North Dakota and MT. This system may\nsupport a few isolated showers or storms across NW SD in the \nafternoon, continued a low pop for this. A separate weak impulse \nmay also support a shower or storm across northeast WY in the \nevening , but the chances for any convection making it into the FA\nare very slim and have left pops out. Main item of concern will \nbe the large ridge of high pressure that will build into the \nregion. Upper ridge will shift east Sat with very hot temps \nexpected. Highs will reach 100 or higher for most locations on the\nPlains, supporting adv level heat index readings. Low level \nmoisture will deplete some with mixing, but sustained southerly \nflow will prevent the BL from drying out too much most places. \nThis will help keep heat index readings higher, esp over central \nSD. Heat looks to persist most of next week although highs will \ntrend more toward the mid and upper 90s as opposed to the 100s \nlike this weekend. Have issued a heat adv through Sunday when the \ncore of he heat is expected. The adv will be marginal out in \nnortheast WY where very dry BL conds and slightly lower temps will\nkeep heat index values in the 95 to 100 range. In addition to the\nheat, expect near daily TS chances as monsoon moisture advects \naround the NW side of the ridge. This includes Sat when a stronger\nmonsoon wave will advect around the ridge in SW flow and into the\nFA, supporting high based TS chances. Gusty winds will be \npossible with any thunderstorms in this period given very high \nbased nature and resultant inverted-V profiles per drying BL. Sct \nwind gusts over 50 mph (likely higher in stronger cells) will be \npossible give DCAPE of 1500-2000 J/KG. Not much rain expected with\nthese cells, which will support critical fire weather conds when \ncoupled with dry fuels and low RH. Ridge will retrograde back west\nsome by mid next week, supporting slightly cooler but still hot \ntemps, with isold-sct TS chances continuing as the lee trough \ninteracts will passing impulses.",
